1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,800
which went on for nearly a quarter of an hour and put an end to any chance of

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,479
discussion.

3
00:00:08,479 --> 00:00:13,640
Afterwards, Squealer was sent round the farm to explain the new arrangement to the others.

4
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:18,479
"Comrades, I trust that every animal here appreciates the sacrifice that

5
00:00:18,479 --> 00:00:23,439
Comrade Napoleon has made in taking this extra labor upon himself.

6
00:00:23,439 --> 00:00:29,880
Do not imagine, comrades, that leadership is a pleasure. On the contrary, it is a deep and heavy

7
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,439
responsibility. No one believes more firmly than Comrade Napoleon that all

8
00:00:35,439 --> 00:00:40,319
animals are equal. He would be only too happy to let you make your decisions for

9
00:00:40,319 --> 00:00:45,800
yourselves, but sometimes you might make the wrong decisions, comrades, and then

10
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,359
where should we be?

11
00:00:47,359 --> 00:00:51,560
Suppose you had decided to follow Snowball with his moonshine of

12
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:58,000
windmills, Snowball, who, as we now know, was no better than a criminal.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,199
He fought bravely at the Battle of the Cowshed.

14
00:01:01,199 --> 00:01:07,000
"Bravery is not enough. Loyalty and obedience are more important. And as to

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,680
the Battle of the Cowshed, I believe the time will come when we shall find that

16
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:15,319
Snowball's part in it was much exaggerated.

17
00:01:15,319 --> 00:01:21,640
Discipline, comrades, iron discipline, that is the watchword for today. One

18
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:29,279
false step and our enemies would be upon us. Surely, comrades, you do not want Jones back.

19
00:01:29,279 --> 00:01:32,439
>> Once again, this argument was unanswerable.

20
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:36,760
Certainly, the animals did not want Jones back. If the holding of debates on

21
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:42,279
Sunday mornings was liable to bring him back, then the debates must stop.

22
00:01:42,279 --> 00:01:48,760
Boxer, who had now had time to think things over, voiced the general feeling by saying,

23
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:52,760
>> "If comrade Napoleon says it, it must be right."

24
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:58,000
>> And from then on, he adopted the maxim, "Napoleon is always right."
